ALGORITHM PHPFormValidation

START

1. Receive form data from the user.

2. Initialize an empty error list.

3. Read:
       Name
       Email
       Password

4. Remove unnecessary spaces from the input.

5. Check whether Name is empty.

6. IF Name is empty THEN
       Add "Name is required" to error list.
   END IF

7. Check whether Email is empty.

8. IF Email is empty THEN
       Add "Email is required" to error list.
   ELSE
       Check whether Email has a valid email format.

       IF Email format is invalid THEN
           Add "Enter a valid email address" to error list.
       END IF
   END IF

9. Check whether Password is empty.

10. IF Password is empty THEN
        Add "Password is required" to error list.
    ELSE
        Check whether password length is at least 8 characters.

        IF password is too short THEN
            Add "Password must contain at least 8 characters"
            to error list.
        END IF
    END IF

11. Check whether the error list is empty.

12. IF error list is NOT empty THEN

        Display all appropriate error messages.

        Ask the user to correct the input.

    ELSE

        Sanitize/validate the accepted data.

        Process the form.

        Display "Registration successful."

    END IF

END
